@startuml
title RuleSphere - Communication Diagram\n07. Protected Execution Evidence | UC-24
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam objectBackgroundColor #FFF0ED
skinparam objectBorderColor #496477
skinparam ArrowColor #496477
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 60
object "evaluation : EvaluationService" as Runtime
object "capture : TraceCaptureService" as Capture
object "protector : SensitiveDataProtector" as Protect
object "hot : HotTraceStore" as Hot
object "ledger : ComplianceLedger" as Ledger
object "telemetry : OperationalTelemetry" as Ops
Runtime --> Capture : 1 <<async>>: capture(execution tree, snapshot, outcome)
Capture --> Protect : 1.1: protect sensitive input, intermediate values, output and errors
Capture --> Hot : 1.2a [protected] <<parallel>>: persist full trace tree
Capture --> Ledger : 1.2b [protected] <<parallel>>: persist immutable metadata
Capture --> Ops : 1.3 [capture outcomes known]: record success / degradation
Capture --> Capture : 1.4 [failure/backpressure]: apply operational policy
note bottom of Ledger
ExecutionID, DecisionVersion, InputHash, protected Output,
MatchedNodeIDs, Timestamp and approval/release reference.
Retention: configured 5-7 years.
end note
note bottom of Hot
Retain full protected tree for configured 30-90 days.
No plaintext sensitive fields in persisted traces.
end note
note bottom of Capture
1.2a and 1.2b are concurrent, not alternative branches.
Never persist unprotected evidence if protection fails;
report degradation and apply the failure policy.
Trace failures must not silently change business results.
Reliability, retries and backpressure handling require ADR.
end note
legend bottom
  Nested numbers identify calls; routine return messages are omitted.
  <<async>> does not block the business response; <<parallel>> marks concurrent sends.
  [condition] guards a message. No broker or storage technology is mandated.
endlegend
@enduml
